module gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.accepted_source_emits_uncompilable_target

import std.types { NonEmptyStr }
import gunbc.recurring_failure_mode { RecurringFailureMode }

data accepted_source_emits_uncompilable_target: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode {
  identity: "accepted_source_emits_uncompilable_target" as NonEmptyStr,

  receipts: [
    "**accepted source emits uncompilable target** (INVALID STATE: a .dag construction the front end accepts with zero blocking diagnostics, whose emission is a target program the target compiler refuses. ",

    "The instance filed here is a coproduct's UNIT VARIANT standing in a NON-APPLIED TYPE POSITION -- a field, parameter or return type spelled with a constructor rather than a type. ",

    "HARM: section 5 silent wrongness on the source-to-target path. ",

    "gunbc says Accepted and hands over a program that cannot build, so the only wall that fires belongs to the target's compiler; where a target has no such wall, or where the emitted artifact is never compiled, nothing fires at all. ",

    "Section 7 makes this the seed's floor and not the target's problem: the .dag graph is the authority and Rust is one realization, so 'rustc catches it' is exactly the outsourcing this project exists to end. ",

    "THE SPECIMEN IS CARRIED IN THIS ROW RATHER THAN CITED, because the fixture that produced it was never committed to this repository (neat-otter-332, 2026-09-01). ",

    "Its emitted artifacts are held by that lane's own receipts; no path is given here, since a path outside this repository is not a citation a later reader can resolve. ",

    "Authored source, two modules: `scope.provider` declares `type Quantity = Time | Memory`; `scope.consumer` does `import scope.provider \{ Quantity, Time \}`, `type NonApplied \{ value: Time \}`, `fn field_as_quantity(subject: NonApplied) -> Quantity \{ subject.value \}`. ",

    "gunbc accepts it. ",

    "DISTINGUISHING FACT, and the reason this class must not be read off the target's error code: WHAT rustc says is decided by what else the emitter minted, not by the source defect. ",

    "Under the NARROW emitter classifier the consumer emits `pub use crate::scope_provider::\{Quantity\};` then `use crate::scope_provider::Quantity::\{Time\};` with no marker binding, and `pub struct NonApplied \{ pub value: Time \}` refuses `error[E0573]: expected type, found variant Time` at `src/scope_consumer.rs:15:16` on `pub value: Time,`, label `not a type`, help `consider importing this struct instead`. ",

    "Under the BROAD classifier the consumer instead emits `pub use crate::scope_provider::\{Time\};` beside `\{Quantity\}` -- the provider having emitted `pub enum Quantity \{ Time, Memory \}` AND `pub struct Time;` -- so the field declaration COMPILES, and the refusal moves to the function: `error[E0308]: mismatched types` at `src/scope_consumer.rs:20:5` on `subject.value.clone()`, `expected Quantity, found Time`, against `expected Quantity because of return type`. ",

    "INDEPENDENTLY REPRODUCED AT PARAMETER POSITION on this branch, 2026-09-01 on gunbc baeabbbf80, by a single-file source handed to the compiler: `type StampMode = StampClass | StampOther` with `fn take(stamp: StampClass) -> StampMode \{ stamp \}`. ",

    "`gunbc compile --target rust` exits 0 with 0 blocking errors, emits `pub fn take(stamp: StampClass) -> StampMode` beside `pub struct StampClass;`, and `cargo check` on the emitted crate refuses `E0308 expected StampMode, found StampClass`. ",

    "One source defect; E0573, E0308-at-the-parent, and E0308-at-the-body depending on emission. ",

    "THE MASK IS THE SHARP HALF, and it is fabricated plausible output rather than a lucky green: the broad classifier's marker import made the FIELD-ONLY source compile by substituting a distinct struct for a variant. ",

    "It never preserved the modelled meaning, and extending the SAME accepted source across its declared parent boundary -- the function returning `Quantity` -- is what exposes it. ",

    "So the narrow classifier's E0573 is this class becoming VISIBLE, not a regression the narrowing introduced. ",

    "GENERAL FORM: a green obtained because the emitter manufactured a target-only entity for a source name is not evidence the source is well-typed, and the discriminator is to extend the source past the boundary the manufactured entity does not model. ",

    "THE ONE .dag-SIDE SIGNAL IS ABOUT THE WRONG QUESTION: on the parameter reproduction the compile printed the ADVISORY `unlisted import use 'StampClass' (referenced but not in any import's name list)`. ",

    "It fires because the name was not found among types -- the front end reached the exact fact that decides this case and reported it as import hygiene. ",

    "It is not a partial wall: it is advisory, it names listing rather than type position, and the field specimen above IMPORTS `Time` explicitly, so it does not fire there at all (see `diagnostic_name_mechanism_silent`). ",

    "RUNG FOUND AT: below the ladder, established by execution at the emission boundary -- the compile accepts and the emitted crate refuses. ",

    "Section 4b's rung-1 mitigations are absent: nothing at the .dag boundary is typed, located or countable about this construction. ",

    "CEILING: 4, structurally impossible, and the reason is that constructor identity and type identity are two distinct modelled facts whose membership is decidable from the coproduct declaration -- a variant name is reachable from that declaration as an ARM and never as a type, so the type-position slot has no constructor that admits it. ",

    "No undecidable predicate is involved, so this is a wall now and not a ratchet. ",

    "NEXT-RUNG TRIGGER, PHRASED AT CLASS GRAIN, phrased as the capability that retires the row rather than an artifact that would contribute to one: FRONT-END TYPE AGREEMENT for every construction whose emission carries a type obligation, sufficient that NO Accepted program emits a target program its compiler refuses on a type ground. ",

    "That capability has one component per mechanism this row carries, and the row retires only when ALL of them hold: (i) type-position name resolution that consults the TYPE namespace alone and refuses a name resolving to a constructor with a located diagnostic, sufficient that no Accepted program contains a variant name in any non-applied type position -- field, parameter or return; (ii) arm-type agreement across a match, sufficient that no Accepted program mixes a coproduct constructor with a kernel literal across the arms of one match; (iii) agreement between the two renderings of an arrow at a call argument, sufficient that no Accepted program passes a function VALUE where the emitted parameter's rendering cannot accept it. ",

    "Repairing any specimen, narrowing the emitter classifier, or adding a fixture satisfies less than any one component and retires no part of this row. ",

    "WHY THE TRIGGER IS STATED THIS WAY, recorded because the row previously said otherwise and a reviewer was right to refuse it: the trigger read as (i) ALONE while the row's population had grown to three mechanisms, so satisfying it would have RETIRED THE ROW WHILE TWO OF ITS OWN DOCUMENTED FAILURES REMAINED AUTHORABLE -- DESIGN section 4b(3)'s grain mismatch exactly, a plural loss under a singular trigger. ",

    "Noting the mismatch inside the row, which is what the function-value paragraph originally did, DOCUMENTS the defect rather than repairing it: a trigger that a row's own prose admits is too narrow is still the trigger the row will be retired by, since a drop is retired BY ITS TRIGGER AND BY NOTHING ELSE. ",

    "RECOGNITION RULE: when the target compiler names a symbol at a type position, check whether that symbol is declared as an ARM of a coproduct in the source; if it is, the defect is in accepted .dag and the target compiler is the only wall that fired. ",

    "SCOPE STATED RATHER THAN GENERALISED: executed for a unit arm at a field type and at a parameter type, Rust target only. ",

    "Record-shaped arms, applied positions such as `List<Time>`, and other targets were not measured and are not claimed.) **SECOND SPECIMEN, AND ITS SUBJECT IS THE CHANGE THAT WAS CONSTRUCTING THE DISTINCTION IT VIOLATED** (quick-crab-396, 2026-09-02, the type_reference_decl_file state-space split). ",

    "v1.tests.claim.carrier_realization_census identity_query_provenance declares a return type of std.coercion TypeDeclarationProvenance and answers it in five arms: three return the bound provenance and two -- IdentitiesDisagree and IdentityUnavailableBoth -- returned the empty string. ",

    "The front end ACCEPTED it with zero blocking diagnostics, emit produced the mirror, and rustc refused the mirror at E0308 `match arms have incompatible types`, expected Rc<TypeDeclarationProvenance>, found String. ",

    "THE SPECIMEN IS WORTH MORE THAN THE FIX because of what the two bad arms were: this change exists to replace `decl_file: String` with a coproduct precisely so that ABSENT declaration identity is a constructor (DeclarationIdentityAbsent) instead of an empty string -- so the uncompilable arms were the exact conflation the change was built to make unwritable, surviving inside the change that makes it unwritable. ",

    "RECOGNITION RULE, and it is narrower than 'run the emitter': a match whose arms MIX a coproduct constructor with a kernel literal is the shape, and it is invisible to a reader who checks that every arm is present, because exhaustiveness holds and only the arm TYPES disagree. ",

    "WHAT THE ROW ESTABLISHES ABOUT THE RUNG: the class is still mechanically preventable and not structural -- the refusal fired in the TARGET compiler, one phase and one language too late, and the .dag front end that had every fact needed to refuse it did not. ",

    "The next-rung trigger is unchanged and this instance sharpens rather than moves it. ",

    "(AMENDED WHEN THE FUNCTION-VALUE INSTANCE LANDED, and the amendment is to the trigger's GRAIN rather than to this specimen's reading: the trigger has since been restated at class grain with one component per mechanism, and THIS specimen is component (ii). ",

    "The sentence above stays because it was right about what the specimen does -- it sharpens rather than moves -- and what changed is that the row stopped stating one mechanism's trigger as though it were the class's.) **A FURTHER INSTANCE, AND IT MASKS BY A DIFFERENT MECHANISM FROM THE FIELD AND PARAMETER SPECIMENS -- CANDIDATE EVIDENCE, NOT A RUNG.** (Deliberately not numbered: this row gained a specimen from another lane while this one was in flight, and an ordinal written at authoring time is wrong the moment a second lane appends. ",

    "The specimens are named by their shape.) Executed by snappy-koi-286, 2026-09-02, and carried in gunbc#9989 (`The function-value adapter, judged by rustc`), which is OPEN at this writing -- so this points at the PR carrying the fixtures rather than asserting paths that resolve on main today. ",

    "SUBJECT: the function-value adapter at the call position in `v1.compiler.emit_rust` `rust_call_arg_function_value_adapt`. ",

    "An arrow type has TWO Rust renderings -- a function VALUE renders through `callable_type_template` as a reference-counted dyn Fn, a function-typed PARAMETER renders through `emit_rust_param_type` as `impl Fn(..) -> .. ",

    "+ Clone` -- and the reference-counted form carries no blanket Fn impl the way a boxed one does. ",

    "The adapter closes that seam, and it fires ONLY when the argument is spelled as a CALL EXPRESSION. ",

    "SOURCE HANDED TO THE COMPILER, three declarations in one import-free module: `fn let_add(k: Int) -> fn(Int) -> Int` returning a closure over `k`; `fn let_apply(f: fn(Int) -> Int, x: Int) -> Int` applying it; and a probe that binds `let_add(k: 1)` TO A LET AND THEN PASSES THE BINDING to `let_apply`. ",

    "GUNBC'S VERDICT: ACCEPTED, zero blocking diagnostics -- and that is established BY THE ROUTE REFUSING TO REPORT IT OTHERWISE, not by reading a success line: `v1_compiler.emitted_closure_compile_host` `FixtureClosureOutcome` separates `SourceRefused` from `Measured`, a `SourceRefused` fails the pair rather than producing a rustc verdict, and this arm reports Measured. ",

    "RUSTC'S VERDICT ON THE EMITTED CRATE: cargo completes non-zero with error[E0277], expected a `Fn(i64)` closure, found `Rc<dyn Fn(i64) -> i64>`, attributed to the FIXTURE'S OWN emitted module at the call rather than to some other member of the closure, and the note reads required by a bound in `let_apply` -- THE BOUND IS ON THE CONSUMER, `pub fn let_apply(f: impl Fn(i64) -> i64 + Clone, x: i64)`, which is the half that makes this the two-renderings SEAM and not a random type error. ",

    "THE POSITIVE CONTROL IS WHAT MAKES THIS AN INSTANCE OF THE CLASS RATHER THAN A BROKEN FIXTURE, and it is the sharp half: a sibling fixture is THE SAME PROGRAM WITH ONE AUTHORED DIFFERENCE -- the producer's result passed directly as a call expression instead of through the let binding -- and it emits and compiles clean. ",

    "Same producer, same consumer, same call; the only variable is whether the adapter fired. ",

    "INSTRUMENT NAMED RATHER THAN TRANSCRIBED, per DESIGN section 6: the opt-in pair authored in that same OPEN PR as an ignored `v1-compiler` lib test naming the function-value adapter fixture-closure discrimination -- described rather than spelled, because an identity under review may be renamed before it lands, and a bare name that no longer resolves reads as correct; three runs on three bases agree, the latest on that PR's integrated head. ",

    "WHAT IT ADDS TO THE CLASS, and it is why it is filed rather than folded into the field and parameter specimens: those mask through a MANUFACTURED TARGET ENTITY -- the emitter minting a target-only struct for a source name -- so their discriminator is to extend the source past the boundary that entity does not model. ",

    "This one masks through a CALL-SITE SPELLING: one source meaning emits compilable or uncompilable target depending on whether an INTERMEDIATE BINDING WAS AUTHORED, with no manufactured entity anywhere. ",

    "So the class has a second discriminator, and it is cheap: RE-SPELL AN ACCEPTED CALL THROUGH A LET AND RE-EMIT. ",

    "WHAT THIS INSTANCE DOES NOT ESTABLISH, stated because the consumer's standing makes it easy to overclaim: the pair is `#[ignore]`d, so `cargo test --release -p v1-compiler --lib` does not select it and nothing executes over it on ANY path. ",

    "It is CANDIDATE EVIDENCE. ",

    "THE CONCLUSION RESTS ON THAT ONE FACT AND ON NOTHING ELSE, and it is written that way because an earlier revision rested it on two, the second being a claim that the `rust-unit-tests` job stood OUTSIDE the required aggregate. ",

    "gunbc#10078 made that second clause FALSE, and it is REMOVED rather than softened -- a sentence reading as two independent protections is the dangerous shape, because deleting the `#[ignore]` would leave a reader believing the needs-clause still covered them. ",

    "The lane IS required now, so un-ignoring this pair is BY ITSELF sufficient to put it on the acceptance path and change what it establishes. ",

    "It establishes no rung and it discharges no component of the next-rung trigger above -- including component (iii), which is the component this instance's own mechanism names: exhibiting a failure is not building the wall against it. ",

    "SCOPE THIS INSTANCE ADDS, stated locally so the row keeps ONE scope sentence rather than two that could drift: a function-typed argument passed through a let binding, Rust target only. ",

    "It widens the scope sentence above by that one position and claims nothing beyond it.",
  ],

  evidence: [],
}
